translation:
Target is the proposition stating that for all types Fm (of sentences), S₀, and S (of proof systems), equipped with formal logical connectives (implication 🡒, conjunction ⋏, disjunction ⋎, negation ∼) and logical constants (⊤, ⊥) on Fm and provability relations ⊢ for S₀ and S on Fm, for all proof systems 𝓑 of type S₀ and 𝓢 of type S that are both classical propositional systems (each proves every classical propositional tautology in these connectives and is closed under modus ponens), and for all arbitrary functions K : Fm → Fm and F : Fm → Fm, if the following six hypotheses hold:
1. (Def1 𝓑 K) for every sentence φ, if 𝓑 proves φ then 𝓑 proves K φ;
2. (𝓑 ⪯ 𝓢) every sentence provable in 𝓑 is provable in 𝓢;
3. (Def2 𝓢 K) for all sentences φ and ψ, 𝓢 proves K (φ 🡒 ψ) 🡒 (K φ 🡒 K ψ);
4. (Def4 𝓢 K) for every sentence φ, 𝓢 proves K (K φ 🡒 φ);
5. (Def5 𝓑 F) there exists a sentence ψ such that 𝓑 proves ψ 🡘 ∼(F ψ) (where χ₁ 🡘 χ₂ abbreviates (χ₁ 🡒 χ₂) ⋏ (χ₂ 🡒 χ₁));
6. for every sentence φ, 𝓢 proves K (K φ 🡒 F φ);
then there exists a sentence ψ such that 𝓢 proves (K ψ) ⋏ (K (∼(F ψ))).

Nothing else is assumed: in particular, neither 𝓑 nor 𝓢 is required to be consistent, K and F are arbitrary functions on Fm, 𝓢 is not required to satisfy necessitation (Def1) or reflection (Def3: K φ 🡒 φ), neither system is required to satisfy positive introspection (Def6: K φ 🡒 K (K φ)), and the existentially quantified ψ in the conclusion is bound independently of the existentially quantified ψ in hypothesis 5 (it is not asserted that they are the same sentence).

